{{Quote|So I gotta leave the ''Ghost'' and go to this nasty-filled asteroid as a favor to Tseebo?|Ezra Bridger objects to Kanan Jarrus's plan to lure the Galactic Empire to PM-1203|audio=PM-1203_1.flac|<ref name="Gathering Forces">{{Rebels|Gathering Forces}}</ref>}}
'''PM-1203''', colloquially known as the '''Fort Anaxes asteroid''', was a massive [[planetoid]] located in the [[Azure system]]'s [[Anaxes asteroid belt]], within the [[Azure sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. It was created from the remains of the [[planet]] [[Anaxes]], which was obliterated in a [[Destruction of Anaxes|cataclysmic event]] near the end of the [[Clone Wars]]. However, [[Fort Anaxes]], a [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Military|military]] base located on the [[asteroid]]'s surface, miraculously survived the planet's destruction.

Within the [[Smuggler|smuggling]] community, Fort Anaxes became a [[fuel]] depot and neutral meeting ground for conducting private business, but [[Ghost (folklore)|ghost]] stories of [[blood]]thirsty Anaxes [[soldier]]s and other superstitions scared most [[spacer]]s away from PM-1203. The truth behind such wild claims lay with a colony of vicious [[fyrnock]] creatures that nested on the asteroid. During the [[early rebellion against the Galactic Empire]], the [[Spectres]] undertook several missions to PM-1203, where they encountered the fyrnock colony and [[Rescue of Tseebo|faced off]] against [[the Grand Inquisitor]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Sunrise comes along fast in these parts.|Sabine Wren, watching an asteroid block out PM-1203's sun|audio=PM-1203_2.flac|<ref name="Out of Darkness" />}}
[[File:Fyrnocks_attack.png|thumb|left|250px|PM-1203 was infested with a colony of vicious fyrnock creatures.]]
The [[planetoid]] PM-1203 was part of an [[Anaxes asteroid belt|asteroid belt]] comprising the remains of the [[Destruction of Anaxes|destroyed]] [[planet]] [[Anaxes]].<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> It was located in the [[Azure system]], a part of the [[Azure sector]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> in the regions known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> Situated at R-7 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]]<ref name="Coord" /> and along the [[Perlemian Trade Route]],<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> the massive planetoid featured a [[Temperature|temperate]] climate,<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> though other [[asteroid]]s in the Anaxes belt sporadically eclipsed its [[Star|sun]], shrouding PM-1203 in darkness.<ref name="Episode Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/out-of-darkness-episode-gallery|text="Out of Darkness" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 11}}</ref>

PM-1203 was large enough to support a thin [[atmosphere]] with light [[gravity]],<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> which attracted a colony of [[fyrnock]]s&mdash;ferocious predatory creatures<ref name="Fyrnock">{{Databank|fyrnock|Fyrnock}}</ref> that evolved to survive on asteroids with similarly harsh conditions.<ref name="Head to Head">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Head to Head]]''</ref> They inhabited the [[cave]]rns<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> of the abandoned planetoid's<ref name="Rhydonium">{{Databank|rhydonium|Rhydonium}}</ref> pockmarked surface.<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger">''[[Ezra's Duel with Danger]]''</ref>

==History==
===Anaxes cataclysm===
Near the end of the [[Clone Wars]], a cataclysmic event shattered the planet Anaxes, creating an [[Asteroid field|asteroid belt]] that included PM-1203 and thousands of other planetoids. While the exact cause was unknown, the leading theory was that a massive stockpile of [[hypermatter]] was detonated when the planet's [[Anaxes shipyards|shipyards]] suffered a catastrophic main [[reactor]] failure. However, there also existed a multitude of more wild explanations, ranging from [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] superweapons to [[Jedi]]-engineered planetary collisions. PM-1203 was a key installation during the war, as it contained the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Military|military]] outpost known as [[Fort Anaxes]]. Republic [[engineer]]s had built the fort into the side of a [[mountain]],<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> which miraculously<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> protected it from the planet's annihilation.<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> The planetoid later became known simply as the Fort Anaxes asteroid.<ref name="Rhydonium" /> After Anaxes's destruction, a large contingent of fyrnocks migrated to PM-1203.<ref name="Bestiary">''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]''</ref>

[[File:Fort_Anaxes.png|thumb|right|250px|Fort Anaxes miraculously survived its planet's destruction.]]
PM-1203's location was a well-guarded secret within the [[Smuggler|smuggling]] community,<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> and Fort Anaxes became a [[fuel]] depot<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> and neutral meeting ground<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> for those who required privacy in their dealings.<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> Dangerous excursions into the facility had the potential to yield Clone Wars-era weaponry, [[Starship|ship]] parts, and fuel. Nevertheless, most [[scavenger]]s avoided PM-1203, citing [[Ghost (folklore)|ghost]] stories and other superstitions. Everyone claimed to know someone who knew the lone survivor of a scavenging attempt into the fort, and their wild claims of the [[blood]]thirsty ghosts of Anaxes [[soldier]]s scared off most [[spacer]]s. In reality, an overwhelming fyrnock infestation proved to be the source of these fears.<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" />

===The early rebellion===
{{Quote|Ezra, when we were on that asteroid, you made a dangerous connection through the Force.|Kanan Jarrus, to Ezra Bridger|audio=PM-1203_3.flac|<ref name="Path of the Jedi">{{Rebels|Path of the Jedi}}</ref>}}
In the [[Standard year|year]] [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Part 84">{{FactFile2014|84|5 BBY 27-30|Out of Darkness}}</ref> [[Hera Syndulla]] and [[Sabine Wren]] of the [[Spectres]] went on a supply run to PM-1203, where they planned to rendezvous with an enigmatic ally known as "[[Ahsoka Tano|Fulcrum]]" at Fort Anaxes. However, Fulcrum had already left by the [[time]] they arrived. To make matters worse, the rebels' [[VCX-series auxiliary starfighter|shuttle]], the ''[[Phantom]]'', was leaking fuel, forcing them to hold off a nest of fyrnocks until they could be rescued by their comrades aboard the [[VCX-100 light freighter|light freighter]] ''[[Ghost]]''.<ref name="Out of Darkness" />

[[File:InquisitorFyrnock-SWR.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Grand Inquisitor faces off with a giant fyrnock summoned by Ezra Bridger.]]
In [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Gathering Forces]]" to [[4 BBY]].</ref> the Jedi [[Kanan Jarrus]] and his [[Padawan]], [[Ezra Bridger]], returned to PM-1203 to draw away the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Jedi hunter]] known as [[the Grand Inquisitor]] as part of the Spectres' mission to [[Rescue of Tseebo|rescue]] a defecting [[Imperial Information Office]] worker named [[Tseebo]]. After arriving at Fort Anaxes, the [[Inquisitorius|Inquisitor]] and his [[stormtrooper]] [[squad]] were attacked by fyrnocks under Jarrus and Bridger's [[Taming beasts|control]]. The Inquisitor ultimately [[Lightsaber duel|defeated]] Jarrus in [[lightsaber combat]], but Bridger drew upon the [[dark side of the Force]] to summon a [[Unidentified massive fyrnock|massive fyrnock]], which attacked the Grand Inquisitor and allowed Jarrus and Bridger to escape aboard the ''Phantom''.<ref name="Gathering Forces" />

At some point no earlier than [[35 ABY]],<ref name="BestiaryDate">{{BestiaryVol1Date}}</ref> [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]]' [[Director of Creature Cartography]], [[Ardis San Tekka]], mentioned PM-1203 in her [[Ardis San Tekka's journal|journal]] within an entry about fyrnocks. As part of her research for the project, she studied at least some fyrnocks in their habitat on the asteroid to illustrate them for her publication.<ref name="Bestiary" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Built on an asteroid, Fort Anaxes was a remote military base used during the Clone Wars. It was no longer used after the war's end, though it still served a purpose as a meeting place for those who required privacy in their dealings. And it wasn't completely abandoned: a colony of vicious fyrnocks nested throughout the massive rock, emerging in the darkness to attack anyone who stepped foot on Fort Anaxes.|The original StarWars.com Databank entry for Fort Anaxes|<ref name="Fort Anaxes old">{{Databank|fort-anaxes|Fort Anaxes|oldversion=20141114214448}}</ref>}}
[[File:PM-1203_concept_art.jpg|thumb|right|250px|PM-1203 concept art by Amy Beth Christenson]]
PM-1203 first appeared without name in "[[Out of Darkness]],"<ref name="Out of Darkness" /> the seventh episode in the [[Star Wars Rebels Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' animated television series,<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels|text=''Star Wars Rebels''}}</ref> which first aired on [[November 10]], [[2014]].<ref name="Insider 156">{{InsiderCite|156|Star Wars Rebels Recounted|''Star Wars Rebels'' Recounted}}</ref> It was first named in ''[[Ezra's Duel with Danger]]'', a [[2015]] junior-novel [[Star Wars Rebels chapter books|adaptation]] of the ''Star Wars Rebels'' episodes "[[Empire Day (episode)|Empire Day]]," "[[Gathering Forces]]," and "[[Path of the Jedi]]," written by [[Michael Kogge]].<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> Original concept art of PM-1203, labeled "Asteroid belt planetoid," was created by [[Amy Beth Christenson]] on [[November 22]], [[2013]].<ref name="Concept Art Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/out-of-darkness-concept-art-gallery|text="Out of Darkness" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 4}}</ref>

While the [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry for Fort Anaxes initially claimed that the fort was built upon an asteroid,<ref name="Fort Anaxes old" /> the entry was later updated to clarify that the base was located on Anaxes and remained intact following the planet's destruction.<ref name="Fort Anaxes" /> Several ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] sources have placed the Azure [[Star system|system]], and therefore PM-1203, in the [[Core Worlds]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /><ref name="BMF52">{{BuildFalconCite|52|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref><ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref><ref name="FirstOrder">{{EncyclopediaCite|The First Order}}</ref><ref name="BattleOfEndor">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Battle of Endor and the Fall of the Empire}}</ref><ref name="Scarif">{{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> but the [[2021]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' later instead<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> decisively<ref name="Twitter Anaxes">{{Twitter|jasoncfry|status/1455675104168484873|[[Jason Fry]]|quote=[Bobby Fuller Four plays] I fought Story Group And Story Group won I fought Story Group And Story Group won (But seriously now, love those folks and I got to place relocated Anaxes on the map and write the new entry. It's all good.)|date=2021-11-02|archivedate=20211102231614}} &mdash; Comment from [[Jason Fry]], one of the co-authors of ''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'', regarding the updated placement of [[Anaxes]] and therefore the [[Azure system]]</ref> established the Outer Rim Territories as the system's location.<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> The [[2022]] attraction [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], set between [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], placed Anaxes in the Core.<ref name="GalacticStarcruiser">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

